  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and winter assistance to influx of Afghans returning from Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide protection and winter assistance, including cash for voluntary return, multi-purpose cash assistance, and cash for winter clothing, heating, and fuel to vulnerable Afghans returning from Pakistan. This UNHCR project provides heating and fuel support ($200) and winter clothing ($74), provided in cash, among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 45,643 people, including 8,714 women, 9,129 men, 23,651 children, and 4,149 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
